,{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"UKpPU6X97oPd-dkCK8cheQ","review_id":"nalR22hW5vAGInX4piGEiQ","date":"2017-09-28T02:06:50","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9428315162658691,"text_excerpt":"Well I came here on the recommendation of a family member and it was pretty decent barbecue. I hate to use the ole adage of I've had better, but I have had better barbecue. We ordered the ribs, chopped brisket, and the carnival with a side of Mac n cheese, baked beans, and corn pudding. As I write this, I still can't believe how much food we just ate Admittedly, one thing that I'm not used to and I don't blame any restaurant in NOLA for this, but I can't get used to the salty food. The barbecue seemed salty to me, but so is all the other food in NOLA. The side order of the corn pudding was very good, as well as the cornbread. The biggest bonus was the $5 daiquiris that we're pretty strong..."},{"business_id":"UKpPU6X97oPd-dkCK8cheQ","review_id":"L_gBeWwd6EGSPbX8Ai01WQ","date":"2018-05-28T23:18:20","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9378801584243774,"text_excerpt":"Very good choice for BBQ, served in a casual environment that offers the best parts of all things NOLA. Located on St. Charles. Street parking might be challenging but taking the streetcar is easy and convenient. Not a fancy venue. It's a big step up from fast food but has a similar layout. They have a bar and a big cooler with drinks on ice. You'll find finishes, murals and other artwork that bring the Voodoo/NOLA theme alive. Everything we ate here was better than merely good. The pulled pork sandwiches come without sauce and the meat is tender and has awesome flavor on its own. Those wanting sauce can choose from varieties found table-side. The corn pudding reminded me of what my famil..."},{"business_id":"UKpPU6X97oPd-dkCK8cheQ","review_id":"w1VVCVWdcJD4Cx8gM4qhFg","date":"2011-11-14T05:39:20","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9375250339508057,"text_excerpt":"I'm from Kansas City, so barbecue is one of my favorite foods. I was really happy to hear that there was an inexpensive place in the city that actually made some great food. I've been a couple times, so I haven't had a chance to really work through the menu, but everything I've had was great! The sauces aren't overwhelming, but all of the stuff that you want is there: good quality, good quantity, simple service, and a lot of napkins. Voodoo is a great and easy place to eat. Get the random corn side dish. It's freaking great."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"UKpPU6X97oPd-dkCK8cheQ","photo_id":"1BQTRPyV32taBiguuh2qhA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/1BQTRPyV32taBiguuh2qhA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8959030508995056},{"business_id":"UKpPU6X97oPd-dkCK8cheQ","photo_id":"sUbTGL7pDcw7wCzyklUFDw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/sUbTGL7pDcw7wCzy